title: "bioenergetic-causality: Mitochondrial complex I dysfunction in idiopathic autism: convergence to a single chronic attractor and causal resolution by dynamic perturbation"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a bidirectionally coupled model of neuronal
  excitability and mitochondrial bioenergetics, with the phenotype-matching,
  inverse-problem, dynamic-discriminator (Table 4), and Sobol sensitivity
  (Table 5) analyses reported in the accompanying Mitochondrion submission
  package (manuscript, Title_Page_Mitochondrion.*, Highlights_Mitochondrion.*,
  and Cover_Letter_Mitochondrion.*).
